[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit"]
[Variation "Queen's Gambit Declined: Albin Countergambit, Modern Line"]
[ECO "D08"]
[Character "gambit,tactical"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "black"]
[Tricks "trap"]
[Themes "win-the-d4-pawn,knight-to-b3"]
[Kind "gambit"]
[Refutes "1. d4 d5 2. c4 e5"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 e5 3. dxe5 { Takes the pawn. Black is offering one of his own to chase after White's king in the centre, but with care White ends up better. } 3... d4
4. Nf3 { Develops and defends the extra pawn on e5. Do not play 4.e3 here: after ...Bb4+ and ...dxe3 Black has [a trap](rnbqk1nr/ppp2ppp/8/4P3/1bP5/4p3/PP1B1PPP/RN1QKBNR w KQkq -) that wins at once. } 4... Nc6
5. Nbd2 { Brings the second knight out so that it can reach b3 and attack the d4 pawn. It leaves the c1 bishop free as well. } 5... Nge7
( 5... a5 6. Nb3 Bb4+ 7. Bd2 Be7 8. e3 )
( 5... Bg4 6. g3 Qd7 7. h3 )
6. Nb3 { Attacks the advanced pawn on d4 again, because it only has one defender. } 6... Ng6
7. Nbxd4 { Wins the pawn back. White is still ahead in the centre and Black has nothing to show for the gambit. } 7... Ngxe5
8. Nxe5 { Trades a pair of knights so Black has fewer pieces to attack with. } 8... Nxe5
9. e3 { Opens the bishop on f1 and shuts out the knight's check on d3. } 9... g6
10. b3 { Prepares Bb2 and gives the c1 bishop a long diagonal. } 10... Qe7
11. Be2 { Develops with the intention of castling. } 11... Bg7
12. O-O { Plan: castle, put the bishop on b2, play Qc2 and use the extra space. If Black leaves the book, win back the d4 pawn with a knight, trade pieces and play on the open d-file. } *
